# =============================================================================
# Dash Client Configuration
# =============================================================================
# The client needs NO environment file.
#
# It talks to the backend with relative URLs (`/api/...` and a Socket.io
# connection to `/`), so in development Vite proxies those to the server on
# port 3001, and in production the Express server serves the built client and
# the API from the same origin (optionally behind nginx). The client reads no
# VITE_* variables at build time; a client/.env file is ignored.
#
# Server-side settings (port, database, JWT secret, CORS origin, SMTP, ...)
# live in server/.env — see server/.env.example.
